From 39d8da9eba2a4229678111aabb64354c189ac19a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:52:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent: make the e2e suites run, and run them against Claude
 Agent (Plus)

Ten tests in `agent` and `agent_servers` sit behind `--features e2e`, which
nobody built, so they had rotted -- run on 2026-10-09 with a real key, all ten
failed before reaching the model. None of the causes came from this series.
And none of them exercised the agent Zeo actually ships: upstream instantiates
the shared suite only for Zed's native agent.

New: zeo_plus_e2e_tests.rs runs the same six `common_e2e_tests!` scenarios --
prompt and reply, a path mention, a tool call, a tool call behind a permission
prompt, cancel, dropping the thread -- through the external ACP adapter, the
path every Claude Agent (Plus) thread takes. `ZEO_E2E_PLUS_COMMAND` names the
binary (default /usr/bin/claude-agent-acp-plus). The adapter runs with an
empty CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR of its own: with the operator's Claude Code settings,
a `"Bash"` allow rule meant the permission prompt never came, so the outcome
depended on who ran it. Isolated, it has no login either, so it authenticates
with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -- and bills that key, not a subscription.

What had rotted upstream, each fixed in place and marked `Zeo:`:

  e2e_tests.rs   the agent ran in macOS's "/private/tmp", absent on Linux;
                 now a fresh tempdir per test, mirrored into the fake fs
                 where the agent is spawned from the project root.
                 test_tool_call read a file outside the agent's working dir,
                 which asks permission that scenario never answers; the file's
                 own dir is the working dir now.
                 run_until_first_tool_call unwrapped a second try_send into
                 its one-slot channel -- Full, a panic -- when the thread
                 notified twice; the first index is the answer.
  native_agent_server.rs   the shared setup registers no model provider, so
                 the Anthropic one was never there; register them on the
                 global fs. "claude-sonnet-4-latest" is not an id the API
                 lists: claude-sonnet-4-6, and wait for the provider's model
                 list, which arrives only after authentication. The native
                 terminal tool sandboxes commands (SandboxingFeatureFlag is
                 enabled_for_all) and its launcher re-executes the current
                 binary with --zed-linux-sandbox-launcher, which a real zeo
                 handles and a test binary rejects: allow_unsandboxed here.
  tests/mod.rs   the same model id, looked up before authenticating -- now
                 after, waiting for the list. test_cancellation used
                 InfiniteTool, which ignores cancellation; the turn now waits
                 for every tool result after a cancel (tools must honour
                 cancelled_by_user, as test_cancellation_aware_tool_responds_
                 to_cancellation pins), so it hung forever. It uses
                 CancellationAwareTool, and asserts the stream closes with a
                 Stop(Cancelled) and the tool saw the cancel.

Measured: all 16 green -- 6 Plus, 6 native, 4 native thread -- with
`--features agent/e2e,agent_servers/e2e` and a key from the session keyring.
Without the feature they stay ignored, so the default suite is unchanged.

Tests only; nothing here is compiled into the editor.
---

